-## Subtopics
-
-### Near-Surface Point Sampling
-A method for sampling points near the surface of a geometry. It differs by focusing on proximity rather than projective initialization from sensors/emitters. [Link](2910-near-surface-point-sampling.md)
-
-### Surfel Parameterization from Mesh Sampling
-A method for parameterizing surfaces using surfels derived from mesh sampling. It differs by focusing on surface representation rather than boundary integral initialization for differentiable rendering. [Link](4501-surfel-parameterization-from-mesh-sampling.md)
-
-### Multi-view Feature Consistency via Linear Interpolation
-A method for ensuring feature consistency across multiple views using linear interpolation. It differs by focusing on multi-view consistency rather than single-view boundary sampling for gradients. [Link](10227-multi-view-feature-consistency-via-linear-interpolation.md)
 
